From: =?UTF-8?q?Ke=CC=81vin=20=CA=98=E2=80=BF=CA=98?= <cmoi@kevledev.fr>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 11:25:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(devcontainer): add missing firewall-docker-setup.sh
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The script was referenced by Dockerfile.base (COPY + chmod at lines
309/313) plus Dockerfile and Dockerfile.php (RUN at project-image
build time) since the v2.0.0 baseline (b996ffd21), but never actually
committed — the base image was un-rebuildable from scratch since
then. Restored from spec : finalize perms/ownership on the
project-specific firewall data under /etc/devcontainer-firewall/ +
touch domains.local.txt that init-firewall.sh expects at runtime.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../firewall/firewall-docker-setup.sh         | 25 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)
 create mode 100755 .devcontainer/firewall/firewall-docker-setup.sh

diff --git a/.devcontainer/firewall/firewall-docker-setup.sh b/.devcontainer/firewall/firewall-docker-setup.sh
new file mode 100755
index 000000000..67c43f8dd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.devcontainer/firewall/firewall-docker-setup.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# firewall-docker-setup.sh — runs ONCE at project-layer Docker build time
+# (RUN'd from .devcontainer/Dockerfile or .devcontainer/Dockerfile.php).
+#
+# Finalizes perms/ownership on the project-specific firewall data COPY'd
+# into /etc/devcontainer-firewall/ by the project Dockerfile :
+#   - domains.txt           (per-project baseline allowlist)
+#   - policy.d/             (per-project L7 policies)
+#
+# Also touches an empty domains.local.txt that init-firewall.sh expects
+# at runtime (whether or not the project provides local overrides).
+#
+# Lives in the base image (/usr/local/bin/) — one source of truth, evolves
+# per CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION bump without forcing project-side re-install.sh.
+#
+# capital-X in chmod = "x only if dir or already +x" — gives 755 on dirs
+# + 644 on files in one pass, no per-path enumeration. Idempotent on
+# base-layer files (already at those perms, no-op).
+set -euo pipefail
+
+FW=/etc/devcontainer-firewall
+
+touch "$FW/domains.local.txt"
+chown -R root:root "$FW"
+chmod -R u=rwX,go=rX "$FW"
-- 
